        "page": 3,
        "modality": "text",
        "source": "data\\demo_docs\\2409.18430_Energy_Levels_and_Transition_Rates_of_Laser-Cooling_Candidate_Th-.pdf",
        "chunk_index": 10,
        "text_excerpt": "Currently, the lifetime of the upper state ${}^{2}S_{1/2}^{0}$ of this E1 cooling transition is based solely on a theoretical estimate of 86 $\\mu$ s [31] and a transition rate of $1.17 \\times 10^{-4}$ s $^{-1}$ . The absence of direct experimental measurements underscores the need for the ongoing research. More detailed comparative data on these three negative-ion laser-cooling candidates can be found in the Supplemental Table I.\nIn the present work, we report the observation of three newly boun\n...[truncated 3451 chars]"
      }
